        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Yes, the biggest challenge i don't even think is software compatibility in most cases. \n\nIt'll be the learning curve of linux, as troubleshooting problems is for the most part going to be more complicated, and since it's linux the user will probably lack the necessary experience to even get his windows software working.\n\nMultiple player games with kernel level anti-cheats and proprietary enterprise software packages that only run on windows will be the exception, but most of those non-anticheat related scenarios can now be solved using winboat."
        },
